  "result": "Excellent! All 173 tests pass. Here's a summary of the payment terms implementation:\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID` - payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Added **`calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`** helper function that:\n  - NET14: adds 14 days from issue date\n  - NET30: adds 30 days from issue date (default)\n  - EOM: calculates last day of the issue date's month\n  - All calculations done in UTC\n\n- Updated **`createInvoice()`** to:\n  - Accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n  - Validate terms against valid options\n  - Calculate and store `dueDate` based on terms\n  - Set `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on created invoice\n\n**Test coverage (11 new tests):**\n- Default NET30 terms applied when omitted\n- NET14, NET30, and EOM terms accepted\n- EOM handling for various months\n- EOM with month-end and leap year dates\n- Error handling for invalid/unknown terms\n- Month boundary crossing (e.g., NET14 from Oct 25 \u2192 Nov 8)\n- Terms and dueDate preservation through invoice lifecycle\n- Terms with issuing (status change)\n\nAll 173 tests pass (162 existing + 11 new). Payment terms are now fully integrated with proper due date calculation for invoicing.",
